BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    In ancient times, there lived two villages separated by a sacred river. The river possessed ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      strange magic: any offering cast into its waters would triple before reaching the other si) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      de.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (    The First Village was blessed each moon with five silver coins. Their elder would stand at t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      he riverbank, deciding how much to send across. If they sent nothing, they kept their coin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      s but gained no more. If they sent all five, fifteen coins would arrive at the Second Vill) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      age-but they would have nothing unless the other village chose to return some.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    One season, a cautious elder sent three coins. They became nine at the other shore. The Seco) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      nd Village's elder, seeing this gift of trust, returned four coins. Both villages prospere) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      d-the First kept six coins total, the Second kept five.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    But one dark year, a greedy elder sent five coins hoping for great return. The other village) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      , overwhelmed by the sudden fifteen, grew suspicious of manipulation and returned only two) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      . The First Village lost three coins from their greed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    The river taught a wisdom: Send enough to show trust and create abundance, but not so much t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      hat desperation makes you vulnerable. And when you receive, honor the trust shown by retur) Tj ET
