BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      The First Village was blessed each moon with five silver coins. Their elder would stand at) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (         the riverbank, deciding how much to send across. If they sent nothing, they kept their ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (        coins but gained no more. If they sent all five, fifteen coins would arrive at the Secon) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (        d Village-but they would have nothing unless the other village chose to return some.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      One season, a cautious elder sent three coins. They became nine at the other shore. The Se) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (        cond Village's elder, seeing this gift of trust, returned four coins. Both villages pros) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        pered-the First kept six coins total, the Second kept five.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      But one dark year, a greedy elder sent five coins hoping for great return. The other villa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        ge, overwhelmed by the sudden fifteen, grew suspicious of manipulation and returned only) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (         two. The First Village lost three coins from their greed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
